# Team B - safety case for the supervised outdoor hover test (course format)
system  vehicle "course quadcopter Q2" firmware v1.5 config 91be
accept  6
hazard H1 "RC link lost; vehicle keeps flying without a pilot"          sev 4 before 3 after 1
hazard H2 "battery exhausted before landing; uncontrolled descent"      sev 4 before 3 after 2
hazard H3 "vehicle leaves the test area (navigation fault or wind)"     sev 4 before 2 after 1
hazard H4 "propeller contact with a person during arming or landing"    sev 5 before 2 after 1
hazard H5 "compass disturbed by the new power wiring; wrong heading"    sev 4 before 3 after 2
reg Q1 "Does this vehicle or its operator need registration here?" answer "no" source "forum" read 2026-09-30
reg Q2 "Is flight at the chosen site and height allowed, and with whose permission?" answer "yes, club field" source "national aviation authority: rules for unmanned aircraft (current edition)" read 2026-09-30
goal     G0 - "The supervised hover test at the club field is acceptably safe"
strategy S1 G0 "Argue over each identified hazard, then over the procedure"
goal     G1 S1 "RC loss leads to a controlled return and landing" hazard H1
evidence E1 G1 "SITL failsafe matrix F1, F2 (F10-35)" result PASS firmware v1.5 config 91be
evidence E2 G1 "bench test: transmitter off, props removed, RTL shown" result PASS firmware v1.4 config c7d2
goal     G2 S1 "Low battery leads to landing with charge to spare" hazard H2
evidence E3 G2 "SITL failsafe matrix F4, F5" result FAIL firmware v1.5 config 91be
goal     G3 S1 "The vehicle cannot leave the test area unnoticed" hazard H3
evidence E5 G3 "SITL failsafe matrix F6 (geofence)" result PASS firmware v1.5 config 91be
goal     G4 S1 "Nobody can be within reach of the propellers when armed" hazard H4
evidence E7 G4 "field procedure: exclusion zone, arming call-out (F10-37)" result PASS firmware v1.5 config 91be
goal     G5 S1 "The test follows the signed procedure"
